\alias{MeasureCptLabelError}
\title{Label-error changepoint measure}
\description{
Percentage of label regions the predicted segmentation gets wrong: the total
false positives plus false negatives across all sequences, divided by the
total number of labels (Hocking et al.'s percent-incorrect-labels metric).

A \link{PredictionCpt} stores only the predicted penalty \code{log(lambda)} per
sequence, not a segmentation. This measure re-derives the model path each
penalty selects (via the shared label-error pipeline in \code{cpt_label_errors()}),
reads off the model at that penalty, and counts its label errors. It therefore
declares \code{"requires_task"} (to read the sequences and labels) and
\code{"requires_learner"} (to read the \code{Kmax} complexity cap the path was fit
under).
}
\details{
The score micro-averages over sequences: \code{sum(w * errors) / sum(w * n_labels)},
where \code{n_labels} is each sequence's label-region count and \code{w} its measure
weight. Sequences carry different label counts, so this weights by labels
rather than averaging per-sequence rates. The mlr3 \code{average} argument is the
orthogonal resampling-iteration axis and stays at its default.
}
